  "body": "**What happens:** the stand-alone **Trochoidal slot** operation cuts endpoints and a width that the user types by hand, but its depth law falls to `DepthLaw::None`. Nothing on the op judges whether it cuts into the model. Found by M5's review of PR #1585 (pullrequestreview-5899641890), on upstream main 45a76e15 plus #1585.\n\nWith a whole-model (Entity) source:\n- **3 mm below a pocket floor:** generate says ok with no findings. With the stock **rotated** (the program sim refuses to judge), the post goes out. With the stock aligned, the program sim blocks it.\n- **Through the pocket wall to Z4:** generate says ok with no findings, and it **posts with the stock aligned as well as rotated**. The program sim misses it too.\n\nThat second case is a gouge that passes every check: P1 under AGENTS.md.\n\n**Why:** `depth_law_of` (crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs) has no arm that gives Trochoidal slot a judging law. #1564/#1585 added `authored_law` for Circular and Slot only. `uncovered()` in posting_sim.rs counts any fresh, stamped op as judged whatever its depth law.\n\n**Expected:** a Trochoidal slot with an Entity or Selection source is judged against the model like the Slot (`authored_law`: Entity/Selection → Section, Stock → None), so both cases above refuse at the op and at the post.\n\n**Done means:** both repros above (below the floor, and through the wall, each with aligned and rotated stock) are refused with a named gouge on the op, and the post is blocked. Pins go through `operation::generate` and the post. Mutating the Trochoidal-slot arm to `None` turns them red. Also consider whether `uncovered()` should refuse an op whose depth law is `None` while its source is the model, so the next op type cannot fall through the same way.\n\nRelated: #1503 (closed, the earlier trochoidal-slot cut into the model), #1523 (one slot confine law), #1590 (the op's future), #1550 / PR #1585, #1543.\n",
